From 71edfd62996a0d816039c9c1092222f3795fa2fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:15:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] clocksource/drivers/bcm2835_timer: Detect missed compare
 matches

The BCM2835 system timer compare registers use an equality match, so
the interrupt only fires when the low 32 bits of the free-running 1MHz
counter equal the programmed value. bcm2835_time_set_next_event() reads
the counter, adds the delta and writes the result to the compare
register, always returning success. If the counter has already passed
the target by the time the write lands - easily done with a min_delta
of 15us, slow peripheral accesses and an unmaskable FIQ such as the
dwc_otg one - the event is not delivered until the counter wraps,
2^32us (~4295s) later.

On an otherwise quiet system nothing updates the timekeeper during that
time, and once the clocksource delta wraps a whole counter period is
lost, causing the clock to fall ~4295s behind.

Read the counter back after programming the compare and return -ETIME
if the target has already been reached, so that the clockevents core
retries (and increases min_delta_ns if necessary).

The check treats the difference as signed, so reduce max_delta to
0x7fffffff; otherwise a delta above 2^31 (e.g. a distant hrtimer
clamped to max_delta_ns) would be reported as a false miss.

Assisted-by: Claude
Signed-off-by: Phil Elwell <phil@raspberrypi.com>
---
 drivers/clocksource/bcm2835_timer.c | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/clocksource/bcm2835_timer.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/bcm2835_timer.c
@@ -45,8 +45,18 @@ static int bcm2835_time_set_next_event(u
 {
 	struct bcm2835_timer *timer = container_of(evt_dev,
 		struct bcm2835_timer, evt);
-	writel_relaxed(readl_relaxed(system_clock) + event,
-		timer->compare);
+	u32 target = readl_relaxed(system_clock) + event;
+
+	writel_relaxed(target, timer->compare);
+
+	/*
+	 * The compare is an equality match, so if the counter has already
+	 * reached the target the interrupt won't fire until the counter
+	 * wraps (~4295s at 1MHz). Report the miss so the core retries.
+	 */
+	if ((s32)(readl_relaxed(system_clock) - target) >= 0)
+		return -ETIME;
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
@@ -120,7 +130,7 @@ static int __init bcm2835_timer_init(str
 		goto err_timer_free;
 	}
 
-	clockevents_config_and_register(&timer->evt, freq, 0xf, 0xffffffff);
+	clockevents_config_and_register(&timer->evt, freq, 0xf, 0x7fffffff);
 
 	pr_info("bcm2835: system timer (irq = %d)\n", irq);
 
